+---
+title: "Clean Task Core Rebuild Specification"
+description: "Implementation contract, code map, migration oracle, replay corpus, and cutover gates for the canonical Task kernel."
+---
+
+# Clean Task Core rebuild specification
+
+## Outcome
+
+Agentplane must have one canonical Task state machine that owns Task, plan, WorkItem, authority,
+validation, effect, and completion decisions. Repository documents, CLI status, provider records,
+and legacy task fields are projections or adapter inputs. They are not independent lifecycle truth.
+
+The rebuild succeeds when:
+
+1. a pure kernel deterministically evaluates every canonical transition;
+2. every mutation is bound to one task, plan revision, WorkItem, authority envelope, state
+   fingerprint, implementation identity, and idempotency key;
+3. legacy tasks migrate once with byte-exact backup, deterministic classification, readback, replay,
+   and rollback evidence;
+4. all production routing, verification, evaluation, completion, and effect scheduling use canonical
+   state only;
+5. self-hosting, crash recovery, repository migration, and release qualification pass without
+   manual task or journal edits.
+
+This specification does not replace the public CLI, context system, provider clients, release
+tooling, or documentation system. It replaces their lifecycle authority boundary.
+
+## Program graph
+
+| Milestone | Task                  | Depends on | Deliverable                                                                                                       |
+| --------- | --------------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| M0        | `202608291005-K5TG4D` | none       | This ADR, specification, code map, replay corpus, migration contract, and traceability matrix                     |
+| M1        | `202608291006-0AJG13` | M0         | Isolated, side-effect-free canonical Task kernel and exhaustive kernel tests                                      |
+| M2        | `202608291006-2A6BJC` | M1         | Persistence, CLI, projection, migration, validation, evaluator, and provider adapters with replay equivalence     |
+| M3        | `202608291006-255K66` | M2         | Production cutover, corpus migration, legacy deletion, crash matrix, self-hosting, and release-readiness evidence |
+| Root      | `202608291005-33PHG4` | M3         | Program completion record; it owns no implementation checkout                                                     |
+
+Only M0 is ready initially. A later milestone becomes ready only after the previous milestone is
+integrated and its acceptance evidence is read back from the exact hosted head.
+
+The 0.7.8 release lane is independent. It may continue from its own exact source SHA, but neither its
+task artifacts nor its worktrees are copied into this program. A semantic dependency discovered
+during M0 or M1 must be added explicitly through AgentPlane rather than inferred from chronology.
+
+## Current code map
+
+The map names ownership at the start of M0. M1 may choose narrower files, but it must preserve these
+boundaries.
+
